 ## Overview
-A GPU-based ray traversal method for Sparse Voxel Directed Acyclic Graphs (SVDAGs) designed for visibility queries (shadows, ambient occlusion) and primary ray intersection. It simplifies the standard SVO traversal loop by eliminating contour intersection tests and distance maintenance, leveraging the DAG's structure to traverse voxels in ray order. It extends beam optimization to soft shadows by determining conservative intersection intervals via reverse beam tracing.
+A GPU-based ray traversal method for Sparse Voxel Directed Acyclic Graphs (SVDAGs) designed for visibility queries (shadows, ambient occlusion) and primary ray intersection [S1]. It simplifies the standard SVO traversal loop by eliminating contour intersection tests and distance maintenance, leveraging the DAG's structure to traverse voxels in ray order [S1]. It extends beam optimization to soft shadows by determining conservative intersection intervals via reverse beam tracing [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** A Sparse Voxel DAG representing geometry; ray origin and direction (primary rays) or view-sample position and light direction (shadow rays); a traditional SVO structure containing material information (for primary ray shading).
-**Outputs:** Hit points (for primary rays) or occlusion values (for shadows/AO).
